WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.840
Happy Valentine's day, thugs.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.820
Today, we searchin for some muthaf**kin truth with "Oedipus The King" by Sophocles.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.420
Man, it is rainin sh*t on the
kingdom of Thebes.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:28.460
A plague been killin homies by the stack, and now errybody askin King Oedipus what he gonna do bout it.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.740
When word comes from da Oracle of Apollo,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.220
Oedipus finds out that the murderer of the old king, Laius, is in town.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.960
And if he wanna save his people from the plague, dat fool has got to go.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:46.280
When da blind prophet, Tiresias, swangs in to Thebes, Oedipus ask dis fool, "Who dis mystery killa be?"

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.040
Since Mr. T pities dat fool, he aint wanna tell him the cold truth.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.280
Oedpius be like, “Man, cut the
bullsh** and start talkin, fool.”

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.780
So, Tiresias oblige a brotha and say that Oedipus smoked the ol' king.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.040
Oedipus all like, “What you say?!"

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.090
Tired of gettin called out, dat blind prophet starts runnin his mouth:

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.240
“Yo Oedipus, stop frontin. You don’t even know who your parents are.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.680
And when you do find da truth, it’s gonna
be lights out, playboy."

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.900
Then, Oedipus’s hunny, Jocasta, tell
him not to pay that hater no mind.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:22.300
First off, Laius was killed by a crew of gang bangers. And second, some prophecies don’t mean sh*t.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.160
Laius was supposed to be murked by his own son, so he and Jocasta tossed dat baby.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.680
S’all good now, right?

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.460
But after Jocasta describes where
Laius got shanked, Oeddy be like,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:39.020
“Oh, sh*t. Now dat you mention it, maybe I did kill dis fool. My bad.”

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:44.860
Back in the day, Oedipus cruised over to Apollo’s Oracle and heard that he was gonna murk his own daddy

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.220
and pork his mama.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.640
So, our boy flips sh*t and bounces outta Corinth, never to return.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.480
On the way to Thebes, he wrecked some haters cuz they got all up in his grill.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.579
Turns out, one of those haters was Laius!

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:03.399
Then, Oedipus gets the word from a messenger that Corinth wasn’t actually his original hood.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:08.460
Naw, Baby Oed was found chillin near a mountain. And according some nappy-ass shepherd,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.520
Lauis’s son was dropped off at the same spot!

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.240
Oh sh*t! That means Oedipus been bonin his mama!

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.580
His mama!

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.040
And his kids are his brothas and sistas?

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.880
Aww, man...that's nasty, man. Disgusting.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:29.620
So, they do the only logical thing: Jocasta kills herself, and Oedipus stabs his eyes out wit gold pins.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:35.480
Then, Oedipus throws up the deuce to all of Thebes and spends the rest of his days wandering the earth.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.480
This sh*t, right here, is widely considered to be the dankest of all Greek plays.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.820
Even Sigmund Freud, the big daddy
of psychoanalytic theory,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:51.220
say errybody got such a hard-on for this play, cuz we all just like Oedipus —

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:56.560
"his destiny moves us only because it might have been ours — because the oracle laid the same curse upon us

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.660
before our birth as upon him.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.920
It is the fate of all of us, perhaps, to direct our first sexual impulse towards our mother

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:11.200
and our first hatred and our first murderous wish against our father. Our dreams convince us that this is so."

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.940
Lemme lay this on ya, playboy.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.780
Sophocles droppin images of knowledge and ingance on yo bitch ass like you ain’t even know.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:23.820
For example, Oedipus’s name recalls the Greek word “oida” which means “I know,” or “I have seen.”

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.680
Ever since showin out by solvin da riddle of the sphinx,

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.520
King Oeddy been gettin mad props for droppin knowledge on all dem Theben suckas.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.780
And now he got a big ol’ head cuz of it.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.900
But after gettin bitch-slapped by the truth, our boy recognize that he don’t know a damn thing.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.320
So, Sophocles spittin some top rank
paradox up in here.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.380
When Oedipus had his eyes, he couldn’t recognize the truth.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.640
But when dat fool blind as Tiresias, he can finally see what’s up.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.810
That’s a big-ass reversal son.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:58.410
In fact, Aristotle was all up on dis play's nuts cuz of dat swole reversal, or "peripeteia," in ancient Greek.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:02.310
Cuz the playa who was askin da question, ended up being da answer;

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:06.180
the doc who was searchin for the cure, ended up bein the sickness.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:10.790
In a situation that f**ked up, it’s hard to believe the gods ain’t got his ass on a leash.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:16.160
